2. Empathy becomes computational

This is where your “weaponize empathy” becomes more than metaphor.

Normal sentiment analysis says:

People feel bullish.

Our system asks:

What would this actor believe, given what they can observe, what they need, what they fear, and what actions are available to them?

Formally:

B_{i,t}
=
f(
O_{i,t},
M_i,
I_i,
C_i
)

where:

* O = observations
* M = internal model
* I = incentives
* C = constraints

Then:

a_{i,t}
\sim
\pi_i(B_{i,t})

Those actions interact.

And price emerges from the interaction rather than being directly guessed:

P_{t+1}
=
G(
a_{1,t},
a_{2,t},
\dots,
a_{n,t},
\text{market structure}
)

Now empathy has been compiled into agent simulation.

