4. Price becomes a sensor

This may be the strongest conceptual inversion.

We should not treat price exclusively as the thing we’re trying to predict.

Price is also one of the world’s sensors.

\Delta P_t

tells us something about what the aggregate system just learned.

So Pantheon observes:

Our model expected:
+1.2%
Reality:
-4.7%

Do not merely mark:

WRONG

Ask:

Which internal model failed?

That’s the Broken-Rhyme Detector.

Maybe:

* customers reacted differently;
* the market cared about margins rather than revenue;
* positioning was more crowded than expected;
* options dealers amplified movement;
* management credibility changed;
* an unseen variable dominates our model.

The error becomes training material.

\boxed{
\text{bad prediction}
\rightarrow
\text{valuable delta}
}

