13. The non-negotiable guardrails

This business actually gets stronger if these are constitutional:

Public/authorized information only.

No material nonpublic information.

No manipulation.

No fake narratives.

No coordinated pumping.

No pretending probabilities are certainties.

Timestamp predictions before outcomes.

Preserve failed predictions.

Separate:

\text{observation}

from:

\text{inference}

from:

\text{speculation}

The system’s credibility compounds exactly because it cannot quietly rewrite its past.

